00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.420
You leave it in your pot.
你把它留在壶里。

488
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:42.480
That's right.
没错。

489
00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.780
I said that the scene could be called something else.
我说过这个场景可以换个名字。

490
00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:45.680
What could it be called?
可以叫什么？

491
00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:50.420
Instead of what's inside the teapot, it could be called Jim's Got It Bad.
与其叫“茶壶里装了什么”，不如叫“吉姆陷得太深”。

492
00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:51.500
Oh.
噢。

493
00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:56.360
Because he saved two sauce packets from a few years ago.
因为他留着几年前的两包辣酱。

494
00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:57.100
Yeah.
是啊。

495
00:17:57.100 --> 00:18:00.160
That's someone who has got it really bad.
那才叫陷得真的太深了。

496
00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:00.680
Okay.
好吧。

497
00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:01.580
I – yeah.
我——是啊。

498
00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:02.120
Yeah.
是啊。

499
00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:08.900
I feel like that could have been written a little differently where Jim could have said a couple of years ago, Pam did this thing with the hot sauce,
我觉得那段戏可以写得稍微不同一点，吉姆可以说几年前帕姆做过关于辣酱的那件事，

500
00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:13.000
and therefore I am putting a packet of hot sauce in there.
所以我在里面放了一包辣酱。

501
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.120
The fact that he saved the two packets of hot sauce.
他留着那两包辣酱的事实。

502
00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.280
For years.
留了好多年。

503
00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:18.900
For years.
好多年了。

504
00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:19.160
Yeah.
是啊。

505
00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:19.960
He loves you.
他爱你。

506
00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:20.600
He loves you.
他爱你。

507
00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:21.280
Okay, go on.
好吧，继续说。

508
00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:21.560
He definitely does.
他绝对是爱你的。

509
00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:21.820
All right.
好吧。

510
00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.640
Well, I do have a lot to say about the teapot.
嗯，关于那个茶壶，我确实有很多话要说。

511
00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:33.140
So first of all, Phil Shea offered me a variety of teapots before we started shooting in many colors, and I picked the teal.
首先，在开拍前，Phil Shea 给了我各种颜色的茶壶供我选择，我挑了那个蓝绿色的。

512
00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:34.540
I love it.
我很喜欢它。

513
00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:34.820
Yeah.
是啊。

514
00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:35.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

515
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.280
A little pop of color.
能增添一点色彩。

516
00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:47.720
The writers also said that picking what this gift would be, the fact that it would be a teapot, provided a major challenge because they needed a gift that could hide other gifts,
编剧们也说过，要选出这个礼物是什么，也就是选定茶壶，是一个巨大的挑战，因为他们需要一个能藏其他礼物的礼物，

517
00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:54.700
that was really personal, and that would be very stressful when Dwight takes it away from Pam.
而且要非常私人化，还要在 Dwight 从 Pam 那里抢走它时让人感到非常揪心。

518
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:59.340
It could only cost $20, and it had to be something that Dwight really wanted.
它价格不能超过20美元，而且必须是 Dwight 非常想要的东西。

519
00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.380
And they said it was not easy.
他们说这并不容易。

520
00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:06.880
They spent a very long time because they knew plot-wise what had to happen,
他们花了很多时间，因为他们知道剧情上必须发生什么，

521
00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:13.320
that Jim gives Pam a gift filled with secret treasures that Dwight also wants to have that costs under $20.
就是 Jim 送给 Pam 一个装满秘密宝藏的礼物，而这些宝藏也是 Dwight 想要的，且总价不到20美元。

522
00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:16.740
It took them a very long time to come up with teapot.
他们花了很长时间才想到茶壶这个点子。

523
00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:19.420
For that reason alone, okay, fine.
单凭这一点，好吧，行吧。

524
00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:21.660
Pam can make her tea at the counter.
Pam 可以在柜台上泡茶。

525
00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:22.420
She can steal some tea at her desk.
她可以在办公桌上偷着喝茶。

526
00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:27.700
Because when Dwight puts it in his nose, I know that's later, but it's so perfect.
因为当 Dwight 把茶壶凑到鼻子前闻的时候——我知道那是后面的剧情了——但那真的太完美了。

527
00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:28.460
It is.
确实。

528
00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.220
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

529
00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.600
I mean, they nailed it, right?
我是说，他们选得太棒了，对吧？

530
00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:31.340
They nailed it.
他们选得太棒了。

531
00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:32.900
And now this teapot is famous.
现在这个茶壶出名了。

532
00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:38.640
I mean, all the time, people are using this teapot idea to propose to their loved ones.
我是说，一直都有人用这个茶壶的点子向爱人求婚。

533
00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.840
I see it all the time.
我经常看到。

534
00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.600
In my Instagram, people are tagging me.
在我的 Instagram 上，人们经常艾特我。

535
00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.220
It's always charming to me.
这对我来说总是很有魅力。

536
00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.300
It's always so sweet.
总是那么甜蜜。

537
00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.380
It is very thoughtful.
这非常有心意。

538
00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:50.200
So we mentioned the things that he's putting into the teapot.
我们提到了他放进茶壶里的那些东西。

539
00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:51.740
Here's a fan question.
这里有个粉丝提问。

540
00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:57.220
Taylor Rilling said, what is the significance of the pencil that Jim puts in the teapot?
Taylor Rilling 问，Jim 放进茶壶里的那支铅笔有什么意义？

541
00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.860
