什么？

1588
01:06:20.390 --> 01:06:21.230
Watch the scene.
看这一幕。

1589
01:06:21.390 --> 01:06:21.970
I throw them down.
我把它们扔下去。

1590
01:06:21.970 --> 01:06:24.270
They bounce straight up in the air.
它们直接弹到了半空中。

1591
01:06:24.410 --> 01:06:25.210
What were they?
那它们是什么做的？

1592
01:06:25.390 --> 01:06:28.230
They were like some kind of plastic composite whatever.
它们好像是什么塑料复合材料之类的东西。

1593
01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:29.250
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1594
01:06:29.570 --> 01:06:31.410
So, when you look, watch it, you guys.
所以，你们看的时候注意看。

1595
01:06:31.530 --> 01:06:33.010
You see them bounce in the air.
你们会看到它们在空中弹起来。

1596
01:06:33.390 --> 01:06:35.730
I assumed, well, that makes sense.
我当时心想，好吧，这倒也合理。

1597
01:06:35.730 --> 01:06:41.230
We did not have the budget to get special breakaway glass ornaments, and there's no way
我们没有预算去买那种特制的易碎玻璃装饰品，而且他们绝不可能

1598
01:06:41.230 --> 01:06:42.670
they would give you real glass.
给你真的玻璃。

1599
01:06:42.870 --> 01:06:43.250
No.
没错。

1600
01:06:43.450 --> 01:06:46.470
So, these things bounced like a tennis ball.
所以，这些东西像网球一样弹了起来。

1601
01:06:46.750 --> 01:06:48.830
And so, Charles is like, cut.
于是，查尔斯喊了停。

1602
01:06:48.930 --> 01:06:50.570
And he goes, okay, two things.
他说，好吧，有两件事。

1603
01:06:50.570 --> 01:06:53.370
One, we need you to stand closer to the wall.
第一，我们需要你站得离墙近一点。

1604
01:06:53.510 --> 01:06:56.890
Like, if you can in the scene, get as close to the wall as possible, because that's where
就是说，如果场景允许的话，尽可能贴近墙壁，因为那是

1605
01:06:56.890 --> 01:06:59.450
the guy is with the soap coming down.
那个洒肥皂的人所在的位置。

1606
01:06:59.650 --> 01:06:59.830
Yeah.
嗯。

1607
01:06:59.830 --> 01:07:01.350
The soap doesn't ball very far.
肥皂喷不到太远的地方。

1608
01:07:01.550 --> 01:07:01.770
Yeah.
嗯。

1609
01:07:02.010 --> 01:07:03.250
So, we have another take.
所以，我们又拍了一遍。

1610
01:07:03.750 --> 01:07:05.570
And he's like, why aren't you breaking the ornaments?
然后他说，你为什么不把装饰品砸碎？

1611
01:07:05.710 --> 01:07:06.710
I'm like, Charles, they're bouncing.
我说，查尔斯，它们在反弹。

1612
01:07:06.710 --> 01:07:07.530
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

1613
01:07:07.690 --> 01:07:08.790
He goes, can you throw them harder?
他说，你能扔得用力点吗？

1614
01:07:08.930 --> 01:07:10.590
I was like, yeah, they're just going to bounce higher.
我说，可以，但它们只会弹得更高。

1615
01:07:10.830 --> 01:07:11.150
Oh.
哦。

1616
01:07:11.390 --> 01:07:13.050
And I was like, okay, I got it.
然后我说，好吧，我明白了。

1617
01:07:13.090 --> 01:07:13.410
I got it.
我明白了。

1618
01:07:13.430 --> 01:07:14.010
I have an idea.
我有个主意。

1619
01:07:20.570 --> 01:07:25.590
Again, the most awesome photo that I have, and it's the snow falling and me throwing
再说一次，我有一张最棒的照片，画面里雪花飘落，我正在扔

1620
01:07:25.590 --> 01:07:29.210
the ornaments and Charles McDougal in the distance watching me.
装饰品，而查尔斯·麦克杜格尔在远处看着我。

1621
01:07:29.530 --> 01:07:29.930
Oh.
哦。

1622
01:07:30.290 --> 01:07:30.490
It's the cooleSt.
太酷了。

1623
01:07:30.490 --> 01:07:30.910
That's great.
那太棒了。

1624
01:07:31.030 --> 01:07:32.770
Michael Gallenberg, our set designer.
我们的布景设计师迈克尔·加伦伯格。

1625
01:07:32.890 --> 01:07:33.110
Yeah.
嗯。

1626
01:07:33.110 --> 01:07:33.970
He took this photo.
他拍了这张照片。

1627
01:07:34.090 --> 01:07:34.610
It was so cool.
真的很酷。

1628
01:07:34.750 --> 01:07:36.070
But anyway, here I am.
总之，我就在那儿。

1629
01:07:36.270 --> 01:07:37.170
We're running out of time.
我们的时间不多了。

1630
01:07:37.390 --> 01:07:38.110
I got to stand.
我得站好。

1631
01:07:38.230 --> 01:07:39.490
I got to get myself to the wall.
我得把自己挪到墙边。

1632
01:07:39.650 --> 01:07:42.090
I got to throw these ornaments, and I need them to break.
我得把这些装饰品扔出去，而且我需要它们碎掉。

1633
01:07:42.390 --> 01:07:44.090
And I have to shriek, right?
我还得尖叫，对吧？

1634
01:07:44.570 --> 01:07:47.430
So I throw them with, I said, I'm going to throw them harder this time.
所以我扔的时候说，这次我要扔得更用力些。

1635
01:07:47.430 --> 01:07:47.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1636
01:07:48.010 --> 01:07:49.490
So I threw them as hard as I could.
于是我使出全力扔了出去。

1637
01:07:50.090 --> 01:07:51.310
They bounced up higher.
它们弹得更高了。

1638
01:07:52.150 --> 01:07:57.170
I shrieked, and I just started stomping on them and shattering them with my feet.
我尖叫着，然后就开始用脚踩它们，把它们踩碎。

1639
01:07:57.290 --> 01:08:00.650
Was that your intention going in when you're like, I have an idea.
当你心想“我有个主意”的时候，这就是你的打算吗？

1640
01:08:00.650 --> 01:08:01.170
I can do it.
我能做到。

1641
01:08:01.210 --> 01:08:01.490
I can do it.
我能做到。

1642
01:08:01.490 --> 01:08:04.770
I was thinking, if I can't get them to break, I have to start stomping on them.
我在想，如果我没法把它们砸碎，我就得开始踩它们。

1643
01:08:04.810 --> 01:08:05.130
Yes.
是的。

1644
01:08:05.250 --> 01:08:06.390
So that's what I just did.
所以我刚才就是这么做的。

1645
01:08:06.510 --> 01:08:07.690
That was just an improv in the moment.
那只是当时即兴发挥的。

1646
01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:08.910
I just started stomping on them.
我直接就开始踩它们了。

1647
01:08:09.310 --> 01:08:11.470
Folks, notice I'm wearing my Sass shoes.
各位，注意看我穿的是Sass鞋。

1648
01:08:11.770 --> 01:08:13.870
Oh, that's the perfect shoe for this.
哦，那是做这件事的完美鞋子。

1649
01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:14.630
I know.
我知道。

1650
01:08:14.830 --> 01:08:15.970
And so I shriek.
然后我就尖叫起来。

1651
01:08:16.090 --> 01:08:16.930
I get to the wall.
我走到墙边。

1652
01:08:17.090 --> 01:08:17.990
I'm stomping things.
我把东西踩得粉碎。

1653
01:08:18.090 --> 01:08:19.350
I rip the box apart.
我把盒子撕开了。

1654
01:08:19.850 --> 01:08:20.990
We got the scene.
我们拍完那场戏了。

1655
01:08:21.570 --> 01:08:21.850
Oh.
哦。

1656
01:08:22.350 --> 01:08:27.750
Let me tell you, ToneLoke89 is going to be very happy because they wrote in with a fan question.
跟你说，ToneLoke89一定会很高兴，因为他们发来了一个粉丝提问。

1657
01:08:27.950 --> 01:08:28.590
What was that?
那是什么？

1658
01:08:28.750 --> 01:08:32.650
One of my favorite scenes is when Angela screams and smashes the glass ornaments.
我最喜欢的场景之一是安吉拉尖叫着砸碎玻璃装饰品的时候。

1659
01:08:32.750 --> 01:08:34.590
What was it like to film?
拍那场戏是什么感觉？

1660
01:08:34.990 --> 01:08:35.930
All of that.
就是那种感觉。

1661
01:08:36.110 --> 01:08:36.410
Yes.
没错。

1662
01:08:36.790 --> 01:08:37.190
Exactly.
正是如此。

1663
01:08:37.510 --> 01:08:41.530
But now if you go back and watch the scene, you guys, watch the first two that I threw.
但现在如果你回去重看那场戏，大家注意看我扔的前两个。

1664
01:08:41.770 --> 01:08:43.590
I think that's kind of from the first take.
我觉得那应该是第一遍拍摄的素材。

1665
01:08:43.590 --> 01:08:44.970
They bounce straight up.
它们直接弹起来了。

1666
01:08:45.470 --> 01:08:49.710
So when we go back up in the office, I have to point out that when everybody decides to go to
所以当我们回到办公室时，我必须指出，当大家决定去

1667
01:08:49.710 --> 01:08:53.750
poor Richard's, Michael gets invited and the look on his face.
“可怜的理查德”酒吧时，迈克尔被邀请了，看他当时的表情。

1668
01:08:53.990 --> 01:08:57.150
It's better than any gift he could have been given.
那比他能收到的任何礼物都好。

1669
01:08:57.150 --> 01:08:57.990
I know.
我知道。

1670
01:08:58.130 --> 01:09:02.790
And this is that moment where you're like, Michael has been just such a jerk this whole episode.
这就是那种让你觉得，迈克尔这一整集都像个混蛋的时刻。

1671
01:09:02.790 --> 01:09:08.450
And then you see this sort of sad, wounded person that just wants people to like him.
然后你又看到了这个有点悲伤、受伤的人，他只是想让大家喜欢他。

1672
01:09:08.570 --> 01:09:08.810
Yes.
是的。

1673
01:09:08.890 --> 01:09:11.950
How much he needs people to invite him to have drinks.
他有多么渴望别人邀请他去喝酒。

1674
01:09:12.130 --> 01:09:13.170
Like he needs it.
就像他非常需要那样。

1675
01:09:13.250 --> 01:09:15.490
Or he needs his gift to be the most popular.
或者他需要自己的礼物成为最受欢迎的那个。

1676
01:09:15.770 --> 01:09:15.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1677
01:09:16.190 --> 01:09:17.570
He needs that acceptance.
他需要那种认可。

1678
01:09:18.150 --> 01:09:23.350
Well, we have Michael's talking head at the end where he's talking about Christmas and gifts.
嗯，我们有迈克尔在结尾处的采访镜头，他在谈论圣诞节和礼物。

1679
01:09:23.550 --> 01:09:25.010
Here's a little fun tidbit.
这里有个有趣的小花絮。

1680
01:09:25.190 --> 01:09:29.070
This talking head was originally shot to be at the beginning of the episode.
这个采访镜头最初是作为剧集开头拍摄的。

1681
01:09:29.370 --> 01:09:29.930
Oh.
哦。

1682
01:09:29.930 --> 01:09:35.590
But when they were editing, they put it at the end because Greg wanted to do kind of a montage of
但剪辑时，他们把它放到了结尾，因为格雷格想做一个蒙太奇，

1683
